    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are positioned for a high-ceiling outing, anchored by **Gunnar Henderson**, whose 81.88 efficiency score makes him our clear priority play. He benefits from an ideal confluence of variables: a favorable 4.32 xERA matchup against Matthews and a significant 100% stolen base probability boost stemming from the opposing battery's slow delivery. While **Kyle Tucker** (67.28) and **Sam Antonacci** (67.67) also present strong value, the aggressive pursuit of SB category gains keeps **Gunnar Henderson** at the top of our priority list. Furthermore, **Andy Pages** and **Kyle Tucker** receive an ambient boost today, as favorable wind conditions at the park add a projected 5% cushion to their output against Lynch IV.\n\nStrategic roster management remains tight, as the threshold for starts remains unforgiving. **Nasim Nunez** (52.28) is the most tenuous inclusion in today\u2019s lineup; while his speed is a necessary asset for our Roto standing, the matchup against Peterson\u2019s elite hold efficiency\u2014which penalizes his SB upside\u2014nearly pushed him to the bench. Ultimately, **Nasim Nunez** survives the cut over available reserves because his speed utility outweighs the depth concerns currently plaguing our roster, where **Jordan Westburg** and **Josh Jung** remain sidelined on the IL. As we monitor the pending status of our lower-order bats, the primary focus is minimizing game-cap erosion while capitalizing on the platoon advantages leveraged by **Drake Baldwin** and **Jackson Merrill**, both of whom are projected for high-efficiency outings despite moderate opposing xERAs.",
